ral Kenyan homestead, a detailed drawing of a matatu, or characters with realistic expressions—require textures and shading that SVGs struggle to do efficiently.What to make as Pictures:Environmental Scenes: A kitchen garden (shamba), a classroom setting, or a rainy day street scene.Avatars & Characters: Detailed illustrations of the schoolchildren or animal mascots helping the student.Food & Hygiene Items: Complex graphics like a steaming plate of ugali and sukuma wiki, or detailed traditional woven baskets (viondo).Technical Rules for Your DevelopersIf you want your platform to run smoothly on lower-cost smartphones and tablets in Kenya, follow these rules:Graphic TypeRecommended FormatWhy?Vectors & Icons.svgScalable, can be animated with CSS, and has the smallest possible file size.Photos & Illustrations.webpDo not use standard .png or .jpg for large images. .webp is a modern format that compresses images to be 30% smaller than PNGs while keeping the exact same crisp quality.How to get started:If you are hiring a designer, tell them: "I need a Figma design system where UI elements, badges, and math counting assets are exported as SVGs, and character illustrations or background scenes are exported as WebP."Would you like to see a text mockup of how a specific Grade 1 math problem (like counting Kenyan coins or bundles of sticks) would look using these SVG assets?LogoipsumSVG vs JPG & PNG: Why Vector is the Future of Web GraphicsScalable Vector Graphics (SVG) are code-based. An SVG file is a set of mathematical instructions that tell the browser how to draw...Cityline WebsitesRecommended Image Formats for WebsitesUnlike raster images (e.g., JPEG or PNG), SVG images can be scaled to any size without loss of quality. This makes SVG great for i...Gomo LearningWhat is an SVG image and how is it used in eLearning?Dec 18, 2018 — Despite having a very small file size, SVGs offer perfect quality even when learners zoom in to take a closer look at them. Learni...Show alli m